 "text": "Hi, how are you today? Oh, it' a small amount of money given as a reward, especially in a race or competition. Do you want to split the cost of dinner? Kind of. Acrylic is a thick paint that looks like it' been painted with a brush, while watercolor is the kind you get from box with few layers. It depends how much you want to draw rather than just color. Acrylic is great if you want it to look like a proper painting, but it requires more practice. Layer two thin coats of white paint first, then start with the background. It gives you a nice, white background to work on. A bit, yes. Now imagine those posters with thick, watercoloury lines, and you' got the basics of watercolour with a bit of acrylic thrown in.",
